================================================================================
Fonts
================================================================================

The demo application and the firmware use the monospaced bitmap fonts bundled
with `embedded-graphics` (MIT OR Apache-2.0): FONT_6X10, FONT_8X13, FONT_10X20.
No other font data is embedded in the default build.

The optional `u8g2` feature can draw U8g2 fonts. The U8g2 code is BSD-2-Clause,
but the fonts are licensed individually by their origin (some are OFL, some are
Adobe X11 derived and require the Adobe copyright notice, others have their own
terms). See https://github.com/olikraus/u8g2/blob/master/LICENSE and
https://github.com/olikraus/u8g2/wiki/fntgrp. Applications that enable this
feature must record the license of every font they embed; see
docs/FONT-LICENSES.md.

Only the test `crates/utsuroui/tests/u8g2_backend.rs` uses
`u8g2_font_6x10_tf` from the `u8g2-fonts` crate. That font is not redistributed
by this repository: it is pulled in as a dependency of the test build only.

================================================================================
Ideas and prior art (no code copied)
================================================================================

Buoyant (https://github.com/riley-williams/buoyant, MIT OR Apache-2.0) inspired
the tween semantics ("animate only when the value changes", "retargeting keeps
the interpolation continuous") and the two-button `next` / `select` focus model.
utsuroui is an independent implementation built around dirty rectangles and
stripe transfers; it is not a fork and shares no source code with Buoyant.

The design document docs/DESIGN.md was written for this project and was used as
the starting specification.
